### 2. Compound-Assignment Audit (§2)

Grep search for `+= (int)(` and `-= (int)(` across `xtGraphics.java`: **0 hits**.

Disassembly of all arithmetic sites in `xtGraphics.class` confirmed that all `+=` and `-=` occurrences operate solely on integer types:
- Lines 247–248: `l += aconto[k2].nhits; j2 += aconto[k2].maxhits;` (integer addition)
- Line 379: `contO.x -= 100;` (integer subtraction)
- Line 383: `contO2.x += 100;` (integer addition)
- Line 417: `contO3.xz += 2;` (integer addition)
- Line 488: `contO4.xz += 7 + i3;` (integer addition)
- Line 625: `contO5.zy += 5;` (integer addition)
- Line 169: `this.cnts -= 7;` (integer subtraction)
- Lines 1249, 1252, 1255: `l5 -= 360;`, `l5 += 360;`, `k5 += 180;` (integer angle normalization)

There are **0** narrowing compound-assignment sites requiring Case A / Case B classification.

